WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:02.500
<i>Question:</i>

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.100
Does anybody here know a "Shinjiro Dazai"?

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.900
Nobody? Well, shoot...

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.330
Apparently, he's a relative of my ex-wife's, 
but I haven't got a clue who he is.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.410
But what the hell, right? I've got a meeting 
with this Shinjiro guy tomorrow.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.420
Who's this guy again?

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.420
The president of the global IT 
company, Shake Hands!

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.500
You came to this event 
without knowing that, sir?

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.790
So if we do a search on "Shinjiro Dazai"...

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.960
Ah, here we go.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.300
He's a car dealer?

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.850
Does he want to sell me a car?

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.810
<b>Shinjiro Dazai</b>

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.810
<b>Gender:</b> Male
<b>Location:</b> Ukyo-Ku, Kyoto
<b>Occupation:</b> Car Dealer
<b>Employer:</b> Sasaki Motors, Uzumasa Branch

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.810
Maybe he wants me to give him a job?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.550
Just as long as he isn't selling religion.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.790
Wait... Maybe it's about that 
samurai sword I left behind in Kyoto.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.810
He wants to give it back to me!

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.680
Imagine if, every time this happened,
 you knew exactly who you were dealing with.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.070
Wouldn't that be nice?

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:04.890
Is this person trustworthy? 
Do they have a criminal record?

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.630
Are they even worth your time?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.870
We've never met before, have we?

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.830
Right.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.840
But I know exactly who you are...

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.090
Inspector Zenigata.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.840
With the ICPO, huh?

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.840
And a very impressive record.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.850
"Assigned to the Lupin investigation," huh?

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.840
This is the new service our company 
will be launching very soon.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.860
PeopleLog.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.870
Hey, Lupin! Pops is on TV!

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.360
He's doing what now?

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.120
With this thing, I can more or 
less figure out what you're about.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.370
What you like to eat. Your pet peeves.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.400
Your work ethic.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.770
Everything from your political 
leanings to your taste in women.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.130
It can tell you all that?

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.630
Terms you've searched for online.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.880
Posts you've made on social media.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.220
Our AI compiles profiles 
based on the massive amount

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.890
of information available on the internet.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.880
Inspector, is it all accurate?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.400
Your expression tells me 
the info's on the money.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.820
Amazing!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.780
I don't believe it...

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.900
The users of PeopleLog can also 
update profiles with new info.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.790
Say, if someone's been nice to you in the past.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.440
Or if they stabbed you in the back at work.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.420
<i>Or maybe they're a womanizer.</i>

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.480
Sounds like the reviews you 
get on online shopping sites.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.930
What if someone posts false information?

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.300
Let me show you.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:49.830
"Inspector Zenigata was seeing a 
movie in New York, last Tuesday."

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.690
As you can see, this bit of 
"info" has been given an F.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.690
In other words, there's a very real 
chance that it's a load of bull.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.190
How can it make that judgment?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:04.700
The AI analyzed the claim 
I posted in very fine detail.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.210
And last Tuesday, you were in Tokyo, correct?

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.200
With PeopleLog, you can predict 
exactly what a person wants.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.690
Do you invite them to play golf? 
Or to have dinner with you?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.680
You'll never have those quandaries again.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.640
You'll see people's criminal records, too,

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.220
so you'll no longer fear getting scammed.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.790
This sounds like an invasion of privacy.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.070
PeopleLog only collects information that's 
already freely available on the internet.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.440
Call it what you like!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.720
There's no way this voyeuristic 
nonsense is acceptable!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.630
Are you sure about that?

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.080
It's not up to me or you to decide that...

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.240
It's up to all of <i>you</i>!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.960
<b>An Outdated Master Thief</b>

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.340
We're here to do a routine
check on your air conditioning.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:39.360
Let me just verify your identities.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.780
The Goddess of Love statue
 is around here somewhere.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.870
There she is.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.510
Quite a looker, ain't she?

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.220
You're up once the lights are out, Goemon.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.270
Understood.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.920
"Thieves are in the shadows. 
All's right with the world."

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.830
Nicholas! Who's that woman?!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.260
What's this?

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.960
Cecilia! What are you doing here?

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.800
If you're not going to tell me, I'll tell you!

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.780
Carla Redson. 31 years old. A nurse.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.280
And the woman you're having an affair with!

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.680
Another cheater? Which one's the wife?

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.730
I feel so bad for her!

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.300
Well, hell. This turned into a circus fast.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.470
What do we do now?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.940
Guess we'll come back another time.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.320
It's the hot new thing, y'know? 
"PeopleLog Divorces."

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.310
The hell does that mean?

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.500
You look your hubby up on PeopleLog, 
and find the name of another woman

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:08.810
listed under the section marked "partners."

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:11.020
Bad news for the husband.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.980
It uses photos uploaded by third parties...

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.230
...to find out who's cheating on who.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.750
Lupin III?!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.370
He's a thief, isn't he?

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.370
Wow!

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.000
Didn't we go through this already?

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.700
Yep, that's me!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:50.410
The greatest thief of our time, Lupin III!

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.320
Over here, officer!

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.100
See? That's him!

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.120
Looks like we'd better make tracks.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.110
Hold it right there, Lupin III!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:02.620
Attaché'd!

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.380
What the hell...

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:09.460
<b>Nice Try</b>

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.700
PeopleLog, social media...

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.850
I'm having trouble keeping up 
with the internet nowadays.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.720
You're talking like an old fogy.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.550
Is Daisuke Jigen thinking
 about hanging up his hat?

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.670
Don't joke about that, okay, pal?

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:36.260
He really did come this way!

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.450
Well, it did say there was an 82% chance 
he'd escape via the sewers.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.070
Man, PeopleLog is awesome!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.780
How on earth did they...

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.860
Eyewitness reports and 
data from our old exploits...

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:52.250
It must've used those to predict our route.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.960
So the AI knows all your habits?

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.160
What a load of crap.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:10.850
Watch out!

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.190
Lupin's on the run

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:12.940
In a car

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:13.940
It was a Gordini

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.150
Somebody get a picture

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.370
<b>Predicted Route</b>

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:22.450
Lupin's heading south on Route 13.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:25.370
He's in a white Gordini. Plate number...

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.250
There's no end to them.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:41.770
Lupin, is it not possible that this 
route has also been predicted?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:45.260
Doesn't matter if they can't keep up.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.350
After them!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.790
Dammit... Lupin...

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.070
All right, let's take a break from 
escaping and grab some grub.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:12.600
After all, we never got 
to finish those rillettes.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.730
Halt, both of you.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:21.000
Yeah. We didn't send any invitations, 
but there's a party waiting for us.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.520
Are the internet rubberneckers 
all the way out here, too?

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.020
The Rat Clan...

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:45.920
I thought we took care 
of these guys in Bwanda.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.670
Guess these are the 
stragglers out for revenge.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.830
And they sniffed out our hideout?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:57.170
Between places we've been spotted 
and local lodging information...

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.170
I guess it's not impossible 
with enough data, but...

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.390
That means this thing's even more 
trouble than I gave it credit for.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:11.200
The world's greatest outlaw, Lupin III.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:17.290
If I can pin you down, it'll prove 
that our PeopleLog app is flawless.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.950
I shall retreat to the mountains for some time.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.430
You sure love training, don'tcha?

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.210
<i>The two of you should join me.</i>

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.320
I am the only one who knows the location.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.230
There is no fear of PeopleLog 
tracking you there.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:49.750
Don't sweat it. I'm a genius, remember?

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.730
Look after yourself, Goemon.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:58.980
What'd Goemon say?

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.580
He says he loves us.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:08.480
I assume they do not require my help.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:11.300
